#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:128
msgid "The theme, explained"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:131
msgid "A design as a ZIP becomes a site; every section of it stays editable where it is drawn. Three short reads, one per reader — pick yours on the right."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:135
msgid "Handbook sections"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:176
msgid "What this theme does"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:177
msgid "A designer hands over a ZIP file. This theme turns it into a working website — the pages, the menu, the header and footer, the pictures — usually within the hour, looking the way the designer drew it. Nothing about it is a mock-up: every page is real, editable, and yours."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:179
msgid "Why it matters to the company"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:181
msgid "Speed: a delivered design becomes a reviewable site the same day, not after weeks of hand work."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:182
msgid "Faithfulness you can check: after every build the theme measures each page against the design — how much of its copy renders, and, when asked, how many pixels differ — and says so. A weak page is flagged, not discovered by a client."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:183
msgid "Anyone can edit: click a heading, a button or a picture right on the page and change it, or use the fields in the sidebar. No developer needed for day-to-day changes."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:184
msgid "No lock-in: it runs on any ordinary hosting. One plugin is required (ACF Pro); WooCommerce is added only when the design turns out to have a shop in it, and the theme’s own shop templates come with it in the same step. Contact forms need no plugin at all."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:185
msgid "Reversible: one button removes everything an import created and touches nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:186
msgid "It learns: every import is written into a journal — what the archive was, what went wrong, how faithful the result measured — and the next import starts from that knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:191
msgid "How an import goes, in four steps"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:195
msgid "Upload the design ZIP on Appearance → Design import. A design already uploaded appears as a card — click it to continue with it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:197
msgid "The upload form with an already-uploaded design below it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:198
msgid "Step 1 — the upload form, with designs already on the server listed under it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:204
msgid "Choose. The screen lists every page the build will make, the language, and — when the archive carries more than one site — a box per site. Pick how carefully to build: straight through, with fields named by Claude, or checked pixel by pixel against the design. Untick what you do not want; nothing here is one-way."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:206
msgid "The build panel: conversion mode, language picker, the archive’s sites, and the list of pages the build will make"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:207
msgid "Step 2 — mode, language, which of the archive’s sites, and exactly which pages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:212
msgid "Build. It runs on the server; the tab can be closed. The screen narrates every step, shows a progress bar, and flags anything worth checking."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:216
msgid "Review and publish. The pages arrive as drafts with View and Edit beside each; publishing sets the front page and the menu for you. The list below the table says what the build measured and what deserves a look."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:218
msgid "The Pages built table with View and Edit actions and the Worth checking list"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:219
msgid "Step 4 — every page the build made, its status, and what the build suggests checking."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:225
msgid "Languages and translations"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:226
msgid "A design that ships in several languages (en, ru, zh…) is imported one language at a time — or all at once. To add a language later: open Design import, click the design, set Language to the one you want (or to “All”), and press Build again. The new pages are created beside the existing ones, and the language switcher in the header connects to them by itself. The pages already built are left exactly as they are."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:227
msgid "Translating what YOU wrote (an edited heading, a new paragraph) is ordinary page editing: open the page in the other language and change its text. The theme’s own admin screens are translation-ready too — a translation file per language under languages/ is all they need."
msgstr ""

